course: dictionary
lesson: 6594
title: Nocturnal: active at night
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Nocturnal means active at night. A nocturnal animal sleeps in the day and wakes up when it gets dark. «The nocturnal house swaps day and night: lights are dim in the zoo's daytime and bright at night» gives you the clue. Swapping day and night is what the house does, so nocturnal must be linked to night.
explain: The opposite of nocturnal is diurnal, which means active in the day. Owls, bats, hedgehogs, foxes, badgers and possums are nocturnal animals, and they have special senses for the dark.
explain: Nocturnal can also describe things that happen at night, like a nocturnal walk or nocturnal noises. Test your meaning by swapping it in: «Go into the dark nocturnal room» makes sense as a dark room for animals that are awake at night.
fact: Nocturnal means active at night and asleep during the day.
fact: «Diurnal» means active in the day, the opposite of nocturnal.
fact: «The kakapo is a flightless, nocturnal New Zealand parrot, the heaviest in the world.»
fact: A nocturnal walk is a walk at night, and nocturnal noises are sounds heard at night.
fact: «Nocturnally» is the adverb: an animal that moves nocturnally moves at night.
exercise: What does nocturnal mean? | Active in the day, like a robin | Full of bright sunshine | *Active at night and asleep during the day | Very quiet and still
exercise: Which word means active in the day, the opposite of nocturnal? | *Diurnal | Nocturnal | Glowing | Dim
exercise: Which bird in «The kakapo is a flightless, nocturnal New Zealand parrot.» is nocturnal? | The bilby | The kea | *The kakapo | The moa
test: What is a nocturnal walk? | A very long walk | *A walk that happens at night | A walk to school in the morning | A walk in the snow
test: Which animal is nocturnal? | A robin singing at dawn | A lark singing in the sky | *A badger that comes out after dark | A bee that works in the sunshine
exam: Which sentence uses nocturnal correctly? | The nocturnal sun rises every morning | *Owls are nocturnal, so they hunt after dark | We ate a nocturnal breakfast at dawn | I read a nocturnal book in the morning
